{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340644",
      "title": "Setting Up & Using Parallel Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 140,
      "videoOrder": 130,
      "sourceHash": "9bb7bfb6ce4ca61cf368d07bab7b4ac995f5dffad35ed2a0bb6171e97254ef79",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "Up to this point, we mostly used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "what we already knew from the essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "Now we're going to add a new kind of route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "a new routing pattern to this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 21,
          "en": "We're going to add a parallel route or parallel routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "to this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "And for that, I'll start by adding a new standard page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "to this application, which should act as a sibling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "to the news page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "So I want to add a new path to this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 38.37,
          "en": "and that path should be /archive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.37,
          "end": 41.793,
          "en": "So here, I'll add an archive folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 46.83,
          "en": "Now, this archive page that I wanna display",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "when we navigate to /archive should however be a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 56.57,
          "en": "that actually consists of two parallel pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "two parallel routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "because parallel routes are something you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "and configure with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "And it's a feature that allows you to render the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "of two separate routes with separate paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 76.83,
          "en": "on one and the same page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.83,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "Now, to set up parallel routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "we must add a layout file to that path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "where we want to have the parallel routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "And then we need to add one sub folder per parallel route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "And I actually set two parallel routes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "You can actually add as many parallel routes as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 104.72999999999999,
          "en": "Here in this app, I just wanna have two parallel routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "Now you do add a parallel route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "by adding a folder that starts with an @ symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "And that's important because that's part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 117.38,
          "en": "of the parallel route naming convention NextJS looks for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 121.47,
          "en": "After this @ symbol, you can have any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 125.703,
          "en": "For example, here, I'll add archive again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.93,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "because on this archive page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 132.12,
          "en": "I actually want to have two areas,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.12,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "one area where I have an archive of news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 137.7,
          "en": "that can be navigated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 137.7,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "by diving into different years and months",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 143.57999999999998,
          "en": "and then next to it, I want to have a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "of the latest news independent from the news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 150.3,
          "en": "that were chosen on that archive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "Now as a second parallel route here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 158.01,
          "en": "I'll therefore add another folder next to @archive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 160.17000000000002,
          "en": "which I'll name @latest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.17000000000002,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "and that will then hold the content that will be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "for showing the latest news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 170.52,
          "en": "Now in @archive, I'll add a page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.52,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "and in @latest I'll add a page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "And since we'll set these pages up as parallel routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 180.51,
          "en": "and since we're using this naming convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.51,
          "end": 184.8,
          "en": "for these folders, both pages can be shown at the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.8,
          "end": 185.883,
          "en": "as you'll see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 189.42,
          "en": "Now I'll start with the archive page JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.42,
          "end": 193.323,
          "en": "Here I'll export a default function called archive page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.22,
          "end": 199.17000000000002,
          "en": "And in there I'll simply return an H1 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 199.17000000000002,
          "end": 202.353,
          "en": "where I'll say archive page for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.57999999999998,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "And then I'll copy that into the latest page test file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 210.54,
          "en": "and rename that to latest news page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.54,
          "end": 215.223,
          "en": "and say latest news page here in the H1 element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 216.93,
          "end": 219.57,
          "en": "Now, in order to make sure that both pages are shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 219.57,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "at the same time, we then have to go to the layout JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 224.97,
          "en": "which needed to be added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "and then export a layout component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 232.083,
          "en": "I'll name it, archive layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "And now there is something special happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 239.7,
          "en": "with that layout component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 239.7,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "In general, layout component functions do receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "this children prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 249.6,
          "en": "well, I guess every React component receives that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 252.24,
          "en": "but in those layout components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 256.56,
          "en": "the content made accessible through that children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 256.56,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "will be the content of the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 260.64,
          "en": "that's currently shown on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.64,
          "end": 263.943,
          "en": "NextJS will take care of that automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 264.96,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "Now, when you are working in a layout JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 272.73,
          "en": "that has such parallel route folders next to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 272.73,
          "end": 276.42,
          "en": "so folders that start with an @ symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 276.42,
          "end": 279.18,
          "en": "then you'll actually not just have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 279.18,
          "end": 282.3,
          "en": "the children prop available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 282.3,
          "end": 287.3,
          "en": "but instead you'll actually have one prop per parallel route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 293.313,
          "en": "with that name you chose after the @ as a prop name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 297.21,
          "en": "So the content of the archive route will be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 297.21,
          "end": 299.97,
          "en": "through a prop named archive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 299.97,
          "end": 302.46,
          "en": "and the content of the latest route is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 302.46,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "through a prop named latest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 308.01,
          "en": "NextJS will add those props automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 308.01,
          "end": 310.02,
          "en": "for that layout component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 310.02,
          "end": 313.533,
          "en": "if it is next to such parallel route folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 314.49,
          "end": 318.21,
          "en": "And therefore here we can then return a div, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.21,
          "end": 323.21,
          "en": "with an H1 of news archive, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.36,
          "end": 328.14,
          "en": "And then below that I'll add a section with an ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 328.14,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "archive filter where I want to output the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "of my archive page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 339.08,
          "en": "And below that a section with an ID of archive latest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 340.35,
          "end": 343.53,
          "en": "which outputs the content made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 343.53,
          "end": 344.973,
          "en": "through the latest prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 347.43,
          "end": 352.43,
          "en": "And with that, if you save that and you go to /archive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 354.75,
          "end": 358.40999999999997,
          "en": "so local host 3000 /archive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 358.40999999999997,
          "end": 361.71,
          "en": "you will see the content of these two pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 361.71,
          "end": 365.16,
          "en": "next to each other or actually on top of each other here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 365.16,
          "end": 367.44,
          "en": "due to the styling I chose,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 367.44,
          "end": 370.62,
          "en": "even though we're on one single route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 370.62,
          "end": 373.02,
          "en": "But since we use parallel routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 373.02,
          "end": 376.74,
          "en": "we see the content of two pages here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 376.74,
          "end": 379.89,
          "en": "And we can now use this feature to build up on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 379.89,
          "end": 382.98,
          "en": "and to make sure that this archive page content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 382.98,
          "end": 387.63,
          "en": "is actually a navigatable list of news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 387.63,
          "end": 390.06,
          "en": "so that we have an archive where we can dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 390.06,
          "end": 392.52,
          "en": "by picking different years and months",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 392.52,
          "end": 396.15,
          "en": "whilst this latest news area will stay the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 396.15,
          "end": 398.193,
          "en": "That's what we'll build next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
